WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:05.509
The Star Wars universe is a pretty complex
place, and it gets a little more complex with

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:10.410
every episode of Rebels, every tie-in comic
and novel, and best of all, when a highly

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.540
continuity-dependent movie like Rogue One
is released.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.789
Every tenuous connection makes the experience
a little richer, no matter how hard the director

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:20.269
tries to hide these things in the fabric of
the film.

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:22.810
Here are a few Rogue One Easter eggs you didn't
notice.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:27.259
Oh, and if you haven't seen Rogue One yet,
brace for impact: spoilers ahead!

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:28.259
Blue Harvest

00:00:28.259 --> 00:00:30.249
What is it with young rebels and blue milk?

00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:34.710
As a very young Jyn escapes her family's farm
at the beginning of Rogue One, we see a glass

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.719
of blue milk perched on a countertop, not
unlike the questionable beverage that young

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:45.539
Luke Skywalker had to endure in A New Hope.

00:00:45.539 --> 00:00:48.530
The blue moo juice also reappears in Attack
of the Clones.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:53.130
Presumably, the junk comes from banthas, but
no one is free from it, even on planets where

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.129
banthas aren't a native species.

00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:56.670
Someone is importing this junk.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.980
Forget about buildi ng a Death Star, just
corner the blue milk market if you want to

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:03.399
conquer the galaxy.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:04.400
Where there's a Whill…

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.939
Back when Star Wars was just a shadow of an
idea in the curly head of George Lucas, it

00:01:08.939 --> 00:01:10.310
was called Journal of the Whills.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:14.740
The concept of an ancient race of aliens deeply
connected to the Force has floated around

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:19.030
the Star Wars universe since the beginning,
but nothing really definitive has been established

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.180
about them … except for that they absolutely
have nothing to with Yoda's unknown species.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.420
Lo and behold, the desert city of Jedha was
actually home to the Temple of the Whills,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.899
once guarded by the blind Chirrut Îmwe and
freelance assassin Baze Malbus.

00:01:32.899 --> 00:01:37.439
The bustling, mysterious city has super-deep
ties to the whole Jedi thing, which is reinforced

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:42.190
by the fallen Jedi statues around the surface
and the fact that it's absolutely full of

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:45.820
kyber crystals, used to make lightsabers.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.719
Jedha … Jedi … it can't be a coincidence.

00:01:47.719 --> 00:01:49.210
And now it's exploded.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.649
The not-so-good Doctor

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:52.860
It's a cameo that's impossible to miss.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:58.070
In the ill-fated city of Jedha, Jyn Erso and
Cassian Andor bump into a really, really ugly

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.030
man and his walrus-faced pal.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:05.240
Visitors to Chalmun's Cantina on Tatooine
will easily recognize the duo as Dr. Evazan

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.670
and Ponda Baba, who try to start trouble with
Luke Skywalker and lose an arm to Obi-Wan's

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.759
saber for the trouble.

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:15.269
Apparently, Ponda Baba could easily escape
a city going totally nuclear, but couldn't

00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:18.840
keep his arms from falling off his body in
a sleazy bar a few weeks later.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.060
Tough break, buddy.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.160
The worst job in the universe

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.500
Directing the as-yet-untitled Star Wars: Episode
VIII would be a dream job for just about any

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.730
director, and as you probably know, Rian Johnson
scored the gig after directing a few episodes

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:35.050
of Breaking Bad and writing the screenplay
for Episode VIII.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:40.230
But he also got the absolute worst gig in
the galaxy: standing next to the deadly, planet-destroying,

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.260
railing-less laser shaft in the Death Star.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.980
"I just want a railing.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.600
You know, one railing, right here!"

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.720
"Yeah I know I've almost fallen over that
thing so many times."

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.730
It's a cameo we wouldn't even know about if
Johnson himself didn't tell us at 2016's Star

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.519
Wars Celebration in London.

00:02:54.519 --> 00:02:59.209
So let us not forget that not only did Galen
Erso built a vulnerable exhaust port into

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:03.070
the Death Star, but he subtly made these guys
lives a living hell.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.450
For the Rebellion.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.390
Budget dejarik and cave monsters

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:10.959
There are a lot of scummy things going on
in Saw Gerrera's ramshackle base, including,

00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:15.280
but not limited to, watching weird holo-porn
of dancing Twi'leks … which only reminds

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.000
us of Grandpa Itchy's dirty dalliances in
the forbidden Star Wars Holiday Special.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:26.799
"Oh, we are excited, aren't we?"

00:03:26.799 --> 00:03:31.940
But amid the many props and baubles found
in the base is a very bootleg version of dejarik,

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.209
the holographic chess game found aboard the
Millennium Falcon.

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:40.319
This dollar store version uses actual, physical
pieces and not the hi-tech, animated, holographic

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:41.319
stuff.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:44.519
Which is what you get when you blow your whole
hologram budget on dancing girls.

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:48.660
Also making an appearance in Gerrera's cave
in especially Easter-eggy form are creatures

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:53.209
from director Gareth Edward's 2010 film Monsters
and his 2014 film Godzilla.

00:03:53.209 --> 00:03:56.890
The director told The Star Wars Show that
it wasn't even him being cheeky; these were

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:59.409
slipped into Gerrera's cave by the crew.

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:01.170
Like father, like son

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:05.230
Like all good supervillains, Darth Vader has
to have a sweet and scary base.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:09.260
We've only ever really seen him hanging out
on giant starships, but early concepts for

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:13.989
the character placed him in his very own Snake
Mountain, by the name of Bast Castle, on the

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:19.600
beaches of an acid rain planet called , where
real estate is probably cheaper than Detroit.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.391
While Rogue One flips the script a bit, and
thankfully, his base doesn't just look like

00:04:23.391 --> 00:04:27.760
a giant version of his own helmet, because
that design was stolen by the Legion of Doom.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.510
Vader apparently chills on a fiery lava planet,
which is presumably Mustafar, the very same

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:37.420
place he lost most of his body parts and caught
on fire courtesy of Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.540
Because there's nothing like building a home
on the shores of the lake where your humanity

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.620
and dignity drowned.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.640
And of course, Vader has to take his cumbersome
costume off occasionally, right?

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.670
We learn that in order to rejuvenate his half-robot
body, he goes swimming in his own personal

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:58.340
bacta tank, extremely similar to the one we
see Luke in, recovering from frostbite and

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:00.200
some serious wampa wounds.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:05.200
Though a sassy wampa-slap is a lot less serious
than, you know, losing all your limbs.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.450
The Rebels connection

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.390
Early intel for Rogue One was adamant about
the film having nothing to do with the ongoing

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:15.000
animated series, Rebels, but now that seems
like a bit of misdirection, for a few reasons.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.050
First, it looks a lot like the Rebels ship
Ghost is spotted among the fighters during

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:23.260
the film's final battle, indicated by the
unique pattern of lights on the rear of the

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.260
ship.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.070
There aren't too many ships' butts that look
like a surprised clown, but the Ghost is one

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.070
of them.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:32.630
Second, the name "General Syndulla" is mentioned,
and unless "Syndulla" is the "Jones" or "Smith"

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:36.850
of the galaxy, that would have to be Hera
Syndulla, the captain of the Ghost.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:41.180
Some viewers have also speculated on the use
of the name "Blacksaber" as one of the Empire's

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:45.200
projects, mentioned as Jyn is searching the
archives and just before she lands on the

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.900
file she's searching for, "Stardust."

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:52.260
While there are a lot of sabers in the universe,
the darksaber is an ancient Jedi artifact

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.860
once stolen by the Mandalorians and then wielded
by Darth Maul, and yes, it has a black blade.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.050
"Blacksaber" could refer to just about anything,
though, from Darth Vader's towering, hellish

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.720
home, to an undisclosed death weapon, to Grand
Moff Tarkin's favorite pie recipe.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.050
Time will tell.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.050
Blasting womp rats

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.500
Luke Skywalker, even though he'd one day become
a noble Jedi, was a jerk of a kid.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:18.870
To quash his boredom on Tatooine, he'd hop
into his T-16 Skyhopper and fly around blasting

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:19.870
womp rats.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:24.560
Apparently, his love of fun is shared by Stormtroopers,
too, since two helmet-heads can be heard on

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:29.510
Scarif idly chattering about how the old T-15
models were getting phased out.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:33.870
Do Stormtroopers go on joyrides, or is it
just an endless nightmare of anxiety until

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.180
a rebel blows you up or a slightly perturbed
Darth Vader crunches your windpipe?

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.910
We hope it's the former.

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:41.060
Red Five

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:46.070
The Rebel Alliance existed long before a shaggy-haired
farmboy-turned-Jedi came along to save it.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.360
While Luke was out collecting moisture in
the desert and whining about not going to

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.920
Tosche Station, a real rebel soldier was flying
around in an X-wing with the callsign Red

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:57.070
Five … until he exploded during the attack
on Scarif.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:01.090
A little while later, Luke would take the
same callsign during the Battle of Yavin,

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:02.560
destroying the first Death Star.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.050
Since, you know, no one was using it anymore.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.970
But he wasn't the only hotshot pilot, and
he wasn't even the boss.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:12.640
The head of the Red Squadron, Garven Dreis,
survived the attack on Scarif and went on

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.000
to attack the Death Star at the Battle of
Yavin.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:19.830
Original actor Drewe Henley came back to play
the role, at least via some amazing CGI work,

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:24.640
since Henley was 76 at the time, and passed
away 10 months before the film reached theaters.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:28.030
He can consider himself in some pretty solid,
posthumous company.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.330
Thanks for watching!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:32.050
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.360
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

